I found nothing that blocks this candidate. The round-2 blocker (a refused Account still being written by the second pass) is fixed, the fix holds up under mutation, and the full synthetic selftest load gives 0 `write_rejected` on run 1 and 0 writes on run 2.

The fake's `activity_parents` total is 103 against 104 in the snapshot. That difference is the one Task refused with `owner_required_unresolved`, which matches the PL's decision that such gaps are expected and visible through exception codes.

Before my selftest ran, an `st/full-selftest` directory I didn't create was already in my scratch folder. I deleted it unused and generated a fresh selftest into a new directory.

